From 1c4d705d4b34bfd5e45169f4b92703f0ede418fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 09:45:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Super-Admin decryption phase (1/2): shared AES-GCM decryption
 capability on the Inventory API

Ports the decrypt side of the Printer Agent's own IFileEncryptionService/
AesGcmFileEncryptionService to this repo - same format
(v1.{nonce}.{tag}.{ciphertext}), same algorithm (AES-256-GCM, 12-byte
nonce, 16-byte tag), deliberately not reimplemented independently.

Named IPrintAgentFileDecryptionService/AesGcmPrintAgentFileDecryptionService
rather than literally IFileEncryptionService, on purpose: this side only
ever decrypts (it never writes a Printer Agent log or outbox file, only
reads and decrypts one that the Printer Agent already wrote), so an
Encrypt method here would be dead code with no real caller. Flagging
this naming deviation explicitly since the brief suggested
IFileEncryptionService as an example name.

FileEncryptionOptions.Key must be byte-for-byte identical to the
Printer Agent's own FileEncryption:Key - a matched pair, the same
relationship PrintAgentTokenOptions.SigningKey already has with
PrintAgentAuth:SigningKey on the Printer Agent side. Explicitly NOT
Jwt:SigningKey and not derived from it - this key can only ever decrypt
file content, nothing about a session or a token, so the Printer Agent
already holding it (by necessity, to encrypt its own files) does not
change what a compromised branch machine could do.

Registered in InfrastructureServiceRegistration.cs with the same
fail-fast Options pattern as every other secret in this project
(PrintAgentTokenOptions immediately above it in the same file) -
required, and must decode to exactly 32 bytes (AES-256).

This is the file-decryption capability only - genuinely independent of
how the encrypted bytes physically reach this service, which is a real,
unresolved architectural question (see accompanying message). No point
gating this half of the work on that answer.

No dotnet SDK in the authoring environment. Verified by brace balance
across every touched/new file and JSON validity on appsettings.json.
Please build locally before merging.
